<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Portuguese Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Portuguese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Portuguese Empire was one of the first European overseas empires, beginning with the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> in 1415 and lasting until the late twentieth century. Through exploration of the African coast and the sea route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> it built a network of trading posts and colonies, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. It intervened in many African and Asian states, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> and Ethiopian empires, and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavids</a> for control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean-trade">Indian Ocean trade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire.jpg" alt="Portuguese Empire" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gabriel Ziegler · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PortugueseColonialEmpire02.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Portuguese Empire</b> that grew from these voyages lasted until 1999, when Macau was handed to China, and left Portuguese as the language of Brazil, Angola, Mozambique and other countries, today spoken by more than 250 million people.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The capture marked the beginning of the <b>Portuguese Empire</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-21">21 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>It loosened the <b>Portuguese Empire</b>'s hold on India.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-29">29 November in history</a></li></ul></section>
